  "slug": "non-overlapping-intervals",
  "title": "Non-overlapping Intervals",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Merge intervals",
  "patterns": [
    "merge intervals",
    "greedy",
    "sorting"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "blind-75"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "this is really asking: what's the largest set of intervals you can keep so none overlap? removing the rest gives your answer",
    "to fit as many non-overlapping intervals as possible, which interval should you commit to first: the one that starts earliest, or the one that ends earliest?",
    "sort intervals by their end time. greedily keep an interval if its start is >= the end of the last interval you kept, since ending earliest leaves the most room for future intervals",
    "count how many intervals you kept this way; the answer is total intervals minus that count"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "sorting by start time instead of end time, which does not produce the optimal greedy selection",
    "using strict less-than instead of >= when checking if the next interval's start clears the last kept interval's end, mishandling touching intervals",
    "trying to directly count overlaps pairwise instead of computing the maximum non-overlapping subset and subtracting"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of `intervals`, each represented as `[start, end]`.\n\n**Return the minimum number of intervals you must remove so that none of the remaining intervals overlap each other.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= intervals.length <= 10^5",
      "intervals[i].length == 2",
      "-5 * 10^4 <= starti <= endi <= 5 * 10^4",
      "intervals are not guaranteed to be sorted by start time"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "no intervals overlap (answer 0)",
      "all intervals are identical",
      "a chain of intervals where each overlaps only the next one",
      "one interval that contains several smaller intervals",
      "empty or single-interval input"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
